{
  "name": "loss_logsigmoid_clamped_basic_001",
  "intuition": "The failure is due to missing required expects keys for pairwise log-probabilities. To stabilize and simplify, use the standard pairwise logistic ranking loss on the margin (log_prob_w - log_prob_l) with a tight clamp to avoid extreme values and keep gradients bounded. Remove optional cost shaping and any conditional batch-key logic so the loss always depends only on the required keys, satisfying static expects while preserving stable preference semantics (lower loss when log_prob_w > log_prob_l).",
  "pseudocode": "margin = clamp(scale*(log_prob_w - log_prob_l), clamp_min, clamp_max)
loss = -logsigmoid(margin)
if weight: loss *= clamp_min(weight, 0)
return mean(loss)",
  "hyperparams": {
